<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Kansas dealers take protection.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Kansas dealers take protection.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kansas dealers said Thursday they were taking three to four cents protection on hard red winter wheat after USDA released a bearish production number for hard red winter wheat.</p>
<p>USDA estimated 1997-98 U.S. winter wheat production at 1.604 billion bushels, slightly higher than the average projection in a Reuter survey of analysts of 1.579 billion.</p>
<p>USDA pegged hard red winter wheat production at 921 million bushels, above the analysts' average expectation of 899 million bushels.</p>
